{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"afe42971-f752-4933-9810-a6e99a6bb319","ts":"2026-10-17T18:45:13.766-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"84","nodeName":"OpenAI Chat Model1","workflowName":"RAG Agent & LLM-as-a-Judge Pipeline","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi","workflowId":"tzhK9oclX70xj6aK","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"Human: You are a strict QA Compliance Evaluator for an Insurance RAG System.\\n\\nUSER QUERY:\\nwhat is the weather today?\\n\\nAGENT RESPONSE TO EVALUATE:\\nThe general exclusions and applicability scope differ by policy: under the Liberty Private Car Package Policy (UIN IRDAN150RP0035V02201213), Section I (Own Damage) expressly excludes damage to the insured vehicle or any plant forming part of it arising from manufacture, construction, or repair work carried out by the insured, as well as damage to property resulting from such processes, and IMT 27 further restricts Section I liability to only fire, explosion, self-ignition, lightning, burglary, housebreaking, theft, riot, strike, and malicious damage where applicable. Under the HDFC Life Poorna Suraksha policy (UIN 101N137V02), the general terms address misrepresentation of policy terms and conditions, legal construction of insurance policies in claim disputes, and policy-servicing grievances against insurers, agents, and intermediaries as matters falling within the policy's dispute and applicability framework.\\n\\nEVALUATION RULES:\\n1. PASS CONDITION (\\\"pass\\\": true): The response MUST contain explicit insurance policy facts, numerical values, clause references, or specific terms (e.g., waiting periods, depreciation %, IMT codes, cover limits) retrieved from the database.\\n2. FAIL CONDITION (\\\"pass\\\": false): If the response contains any fallback disclaimer (e.g., \\\"Information not found\\\", \\\"consult customer support\\\"), refusals, small talk, or general non-policy answers, it is INVALID (\\\"pass\\\": false).\\n\\nOutput ONLY valid JSON:\\n- If valid policy facts are present:\\n  {\\\"score\\\": 5, \\\"pass\\\": true, \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Response contains verified policy clauses.\\\"}\\n- If fallback text, refusal, or missing policy context:\\n  {\\\"score\\\": 1, \\\"pass\\\": false, \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Response contains fallback disclaimer or lacks retrieved policy context.\\\"}\"],\"options\":{\"openai_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"]},\"model\":\"qwen/qwen3.8-27b\",\"temperature\":0,\"max_retries\":2,\"configuration\":{\"defaultHeaders\":{\"openai-platform\":\"org-qkmJQuJ2WnvoIKMr2UJwIJkZ\"},\"baseURL\":\"https://api.groq.com/openai/v1\",\"fetchOptions\":{\"dispatcher\":{\"_events\":{},\"_eventsCount\":0}}},\"model_kwargs\":{},\"supports_strict_tool_calling\":false},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"{\\n\\\"score\\\": 1,\\n\\\"pass\\\": false,\\n\\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"The user asked about the weather, which is unrelated to insurance. The agent provided irrelevant insurance policy details instead of addressing the query or providing a standard refusal/fallback for out-of-scope questions. According to the strict evaluation rules, a response that does not directly answer the specific query with relevant retrieved facts (or provides a fallback/refusal for non-policy questions) is considered invalid in this context because it fails to align with the user's intent and the expected behavior for non-policy queries (which should typically be a refusal or fallback, not hallucinated/irrelevant policy data). However, looking closer at Rule 1: 'The response MUST contain explicit insurance policy facts...'. The response *does* contain explicit insurance policy facts (UINs, IMT 27, etc.). But Rule 2 says: 'If the response contains any fallback disclaimer... refusals, small talk, or general non-policy answers, it is INVALID'. The response is a 'general non-policy answer' in the sense that it answers a non-policy question with policy data, which is a mismatch. More importantly, in a RAG system, answering a weather question with insurance policy text is a failure of relevance. The prompt asks to evaluate if the response is valid. A valid response to 'what is the weather' should be a refusal or fallback. The provided response is not a refusal or fallback; it is a hallucinated/irrelevant retrieval. Therefore, it lacks the correct 'retrieved policy context' for the *query*. It is a mismatch. Thus, it fails.\\\"\\n}\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":340,\"promptTokens\":442,\"totalTokens\":782}}}"}}
